---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Who makes Conflict Protocol, why this field guide exists, and what it will and will not promise."
  canonical="/about/"
  image="/assets/pages/about-conflict-protocol.webp"
  bodyClass="about-page"
>
  <article class="article-shell">
    <!-- Maya HUD Status Strip -->
    <div class="hud-status-strip">
      <div class="hud-status-left">
        <span class="hud-radar-beacon"></span>
        <span class="hud-mono-tag">MAYA AI // OPERATIONAL DIRECTIVE // ARCHIVE BRIEFING</span>
      </div>
      <div class="hud-status-right">
        <span class="hud-shield-indicator">● PROTOCOL SPECIFICATION v2.4</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <header class="content-hero">
      <div>
        <div class="tactical-badge badge-purple">
          <span class="badge-icon">⚡</span>
          <span>SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Built for the moment <span class="title-gradient-highlight">your words leave the building.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Conflict Protocol is an indie game and companion field guide about difficult conversations:
          the pressure moves, the counters, and the exact sentences that help you stay in the room.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img src="/assets/pages/about-conflict-protocol.webp" alt="Conflict Protocol Field Guide Briefing" width="1600" height="900" />
    </header>

    <div class="article-body">
      <p>
        This is made by an indie developer building <a href={site.gameUrl}>The Conflict Protocol</a>.
        The game is the place to rehearse under pressure. The site is the quiet reference shelf next to
        it: what is this move, what does it do to you, what can you actually say back?
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Conflict Protocol is not an AI chatbot that happens to talk about conflict.</strong> It is a game designed around the mechanics of conflict.
        Standard AI roleplay wants to help you, give polite advice, and cooperate. But real-world pressure does not cooperate.
        Conflict Protocol turns psychology into combat mechanics—<strong>HEAT</strong>, <strong>FRAME</strong>, <strong>COMPOSURE</strong>, and <strong>RUPTURE</strong>.
        The AI is your opponent. Mechanically, its job is to bait you into overexplaining, test your autonomic freeze reflex, and see if you can hold your boundary when someone actively pushes back.
      </p>
      <p>
        The reason is simple and familiar: freezing is expensive. So is the instant yes. So is the
        paragraph you write because one clean no feels too dangerous in your mouth. If you have ever
        thought of the right line hours later, this site is built for that gap.
      </p>
      <p>
        The promise is plain words that work. Not a diagnosis of the person across from you. Not
        "unlock your potential" fog. Behaviors, scripts, practice. A field guide, not a personality
        test with better lighting.
      </p>
      <p>
        One boundary: this is communication training, not therapy or crisis support. If someone is
        threatening you, controlling your movement, or making you afraid for your safety, the right next
        move is real-world help, not a sharper sentence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hud-status-strip {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(14, 7, 26, 0.8);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  }

  .hud-status-left {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .hud-radar-beacon {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    position: relative;
  }
  .hud-radar-beacon::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: -3px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--accent);
    animation: beacon-ping 1.5s cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.2, 1) infinite;
  }

  @keyframes beacon-ping {
    75%, 100% {
      transform: scale(2.4);
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  .hud-mono-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .hud-shield-indicator {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--emerald, #10b981);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .tactical-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .badge-purple {
    background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.14);
    border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.4);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
